# dsv41: the embedding table in the GB10's display reservation (TF_DS_DISPLAY_EMBED=1; off by default). The firmware
# keeps ~2 GiB of each Spark's memory for a screen (the scanout carve-out Linux and ordinary CUDA allocations never use,
# MemAvailable never counts it); with nvidia-drm's modeset on, a DRM dumb buffer comes from it, and exported as a
# dma-buf and imported with cuImportExternalMemory it is device memory a kernel reads like any other. Each rank moves
# its whole BF16 embedding table there (1,262.5 MiB, read one row a token by the prompt chunks', the rounds' and the
# drafter's embedInit): copied, compared byte for byte, its ordinary buffer freed, its address changed before any kernel
# or graph takes it, so every reply is the same and ~1.23 GiB of ordinary memory comes back on each Spark. A connected
# display, modeset off, too little room or no card in the container stops the load (fails closed); the recipe's
# start.sh probes both Sparks first. TF_DS_DISPLAY_CARD: the card (/dev/dri/card0). After coolbho3k (emihuang)'s
# finding that the reservation is reachable from CUDA and christopherowen/spark-ds41f's measurements (Apache-2.0).
